<<~ ahu slot=`#/practice`>>
! Art Sigils Practice

Use the shortest expression that conveys the intended work. Keep the Art Sigil about the artwork and introduce operational companions only for requirements that matter.

1. **Articulate.** Write one `<<art ...>>` invocation: subject and read first; specify other dimensions only when relevant. Aim for 1,024 characters or fewer.
2. **Expand selectively.** Use an optional Folio for genuinely independent studies, counterpoints and facture. Keep the contiguous image-facing block within 6,000 characters. No source URLs or procedure declarations in the block.
3. **Assign reference authority.** Name which sources supply subject, geometry, material, evidence, masking, criticism, or permissions. Confirm the receiver can access them.
4. **Specify deliverables separately.** When output dimensions, real alpha, exact text, registration, format or physical support are binding, attach an Artifact Contract. Do not add them to universal `art()` defaults.
5. **Inspect reception.** Compare observed work with the artistic read and technical contract separately. Use scale or context appropriate to the actual work. Record unresolved checks.
6. **Preserve and release.** Keep reversible source materials where warranted. Verify credit, rights, alt text and the publication export before distribution. Stop upon operator acceptance.

<<~/ahu>>

